    "job": 133384927985,
    "title": "Vectorize multiplexer bit draws while preserving seeded datasets",
    "issue": 1331,
    "body": "### Description\n\n`make_multiplexer_dataset` makes one Python-level RNG call for every bit of every proposed example. At eight address bits this is 264 scalar draws per candidate sample, including candidates rejected to meet the requested class balance.\n\nThe generator now draws each candidate sample's bits in one NumPy call. It retains the exact random stream, accepted samples, class balancing, positive/negative ordering, and final shuffle.\n\n### Related issues or pull requests\n\nCloses #1331.\n\nComplete reachable history was inspected across upstream PR refs and fork branches, including intermediate commits: 56 commits and 21 distinct source versions. None used an equivalent vectorized draw. Historical path/rename records were also checked.\n\n### Measurements\n\nFor eight address bits, 2,000 samples, a positive ratio of 0.3, shuffle enabled, and seed 7, median complete generation time over five runs in the same job changed from **0.76748 s to 0.01964 s (39.1x faster)**. Base and patch returned exactly the same (2000, 264) features, 600 positive labels, and complete output SHA-256 digest. This measurement describes the specified workload.\n\n### Validation\n\n- Exact upstream base: `1aee767ef57b84a8191511a08955c583b65de382`.\n- **25 new tests pass on both base and patch**, as expected for a performance change.\n- Twenty-four complete seeded dataset digests cover several address widths, seeds, shuffle modes, class-ratio endpoints, and rounding cases. Separate assertions check the selected-register label relationship, item/label dtypes, output ordering, and preservation of the global RNG state.\n- New and existing multiplexer tests: **31 passed**. Complete repository suite: **765 passed, 3 skipped**.\n- Baseline and patch ran in the same Python 3.11.18 job with the unchanged frozen lock.\n- Complete repository isort/Black, changed-file Flake8, `git diff --check`, package build, and strict Twine checks passed. The repository-wide Flake8 report retains existing findings and is not presented as a clean lint gate.\n\n[Baseline, complete validation, and benchmark evidence](https://github.com/Afloat16/geoopt/actions/runs/43891867287/job/133384927985).\n\n### Pull Request Checklist\n\n- [x] Added a changelog entry.\n- [x] Added regression fixtures and tests in the corresponding test directory.\n- [x] Preserved the public interface and seeded behavior.\n- [x] Ran focused and full repository tests.\n- [x] Checked formatting and style with the scope described above.\n",
