  {
    "name": "numeric-dataset-loading",
    "prefix": "tenth",
    "run": 43893510097,
    "job": 133390720852,
    "title": "Reduce numeric dataset loading cost while retaining parser compatibility",
    "issue": 1332,
    "body": "### Description\n\nThe bundled numeric MNIST, Iris, Boston Housing, and Three Blobs loaders use the general missing-value parser even though their current CSV files are fully numeric. Its temporary Python structures substantially increase MNIST loading time and memory.\n\nA shared internal reader now takes NumPy's numeric-parser fast path and falls back to the original general parser on conversion errors. Missing and nonnumeric fields therefore retain their existing NaN behavior. Values, dtypes, row/column conventions, Iris corrections, independent arrays on repeated calls, and empty-file errors are covered explicitly. Auto MPG keeps its existing mixed-data loader; Wine already uses the numeric parser.\n\n### Related issues or pull requests\n\nCloses #1332.\n\nFull reachable source histories were checked across upstream PR refs and fork branches, including intermediate revisions and the historical `data/_mnist.py` implementation. No equivalent numeric-parser optimization of these loaders was found.\n\n### Measurements\n\nThe exact base and patch were measured in the same Python 3.11.18 job using the unchanged frozen lock. Median times over five untraced runs were:\n\n| Dataset | Base | Patch |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| MNIST | 1.20454 s | 0.15887 s |\n| Iris UCI | 0.525 ms | 0.195 ms |\n| Iris corrected | 0.470 ms | 0.170 ms |\n| Boston Housing | 2.948 ms | 1.454 ms |\n| Three Blobs | 0.514 ms | 0.256 ms |\n\nMNIST is **7.6x faster** in this benchmark. In separate allocation measurements, its peak drops from **228,558,237 to 35,068,071 bytes (84.7%)**. Each dataset's complete feature/label output digest is identical on base and patch. Timings describe this workload; the fallback deliberately retains the original parser's behavior and cost.\n\n### Validation\n\n- Exact upstream base: `1aee767ef57b84a8191511a08955c583b65de382`.\n- **1 of 41 new cases fails on unchanged source**: the MNIST peak-allocation bound. All 41 pass after the change.\n- Tests compare every bundled value with the original parser and cover blank fields, nonnumeric fields, NaN/infinite numeric fields, empty files, dtypes, Iris versions, and independence between calls.\n- Relevant data tests: **56 passed**. Complete repository suite: **781 passed, 3 skipped**.\n- Complete repository isort/Black, changed-file Flake8, `git diff --check`, package build, and strict Twine checks passed. The repository-wide Flake8 report retains existing findings and is not presented as a clean lint gate.\n\n[Baseline, complete validation, and benchmark evidence](https://github.com/Afloat16/geoopt/actions/runs/43893510097/job/133390720852).\n\n### Pull Request Checklist\n\n- [x] Added a changelog entry.\n- [x] Added value, compatibility, and memory-regression tests.\n- [x] Preserved the public loader interfaces.\n- [x] Ran focused and full repository tests.\n- [x] Checked formatting and style with the scope described above.\n",
